.el .ds Aq '
.TH allstar-weather 1  "allstar-weather " 
.SH NAME
allstar\-weather \- Announce the weather on an AllStar node
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBallstar\-weather\fR [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-report\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-temp\-unit\fR] [\fB\-\-periods\fR] [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-engine\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-voice\-name\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-key\-file\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-audio\-format\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-wait\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINODE\fR> <\fILOCATION\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Announce the weather on an AllStar node.
.PP
Speaks a report and plays it on the node with `rpt localplay`, running `sudo \-u asterisk asterisk`, which must not ask for a password.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-report\fR \fI<REPORT>\fR [default: metar]
What to announce
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
metar: Current conditions at an airport, from aviationweather.gov
.IP \(bu 2
forecast: The National Weather Service forecast (US only)
.IP \(bu 2
alerts: Active National Weather Service alerts (US only)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: brief]
Output format for the metar announcement
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
speech: Direct speech output
.IP \(bu 2
brief: Brief announcement format, without the station name
.IP \(bu 2
detailed: Detailed weather report
.IP \(bu 2
aviation: Aviation radio style
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-temp\-unit\fR \fI<TEMP_UNIT>\fR [default: fahrenheit]
Temperature unit for metar (the detailed format always gives both)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fahrenheit
.IP \(bu 2
celsius
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-periods\fR \fI<PERIODS>\fR
Number of half\-day forecast periods [default: 2]
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-engine\fR \fI<ENGINE>\fR [default: google]
Text\-to\-speech engine
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
google: Google Cloud TTS (needs an API key)
.IP \(bu 2
espeak: eSpeak NG
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-voice\-name\fR \fI<VOICE_NAME>\fR
Google voice name [default: en\-US\-Chirp3\-HD\-Leda]
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR
Google volume gain in dB, \-96 to 16 [default: 6]
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
File holding the Google API key [default: $GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY, else ~/.config/speak\-weather/google\-api\-key]
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-audio\-format\fR \fI<AUDIO_FORMAT>\fR [default: sln16]
Audio format to play (sln16 needs Asterisk\*(Aqs codec_resample module)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
mp3: MP3 format
.IP \(bu 2
wav: WAV format (uncompressed)
.IP \(bu 2
ogg: OGG format
.IP \(bu 2
ulaw: ULAW format (8\-bit G.711)
.IP \(bu 2
alaw: ALAW format (8\-bit G.711)
.IP \(bu 2
gsm: GSM format (telephony)
.IP \(bu 2
sln16: Raw 16\-bit signed linear at 16 kHz, for Asterisk to convert as each channel needs
.RE
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-wait\fR \fI<WAIT>\fR [default: 60]
Seconds a busy node gets to open the audio file before it is deleted
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINODE\fR>
AllStar node number
.TP
<\fILOCATION\fR>
ICAO airport for metar (e.g., KSJC); station, lat,lon or US address for forecast and alerts
